[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "King's Gambit Declined"]
[Variation "King's Gambit Declined: Classical Variation"]
[ECO "C30"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "trap"]
[Themes "centre-pawns,solid-centre"]
[Kind "sideline"]

1. e4 e5 2. f4 Bc5 { Black does not take the pawn. The bishop aims at f2 and sets a trap: if White takes on e5 now, ...Qh4+ wins. }
3. Nf3 { Guards h4 so ...Qh4+ is no threat, and attacks e5. Do not take on e5 yet. }
3... d6
4. c3 { Prepares d4 to take the whole centre. The pawn on c3 also gives the queen's knight the d2 square. }
4... Nf6 ( 4... Bg4 5. Be2 { Unpins the knight on f3 and prepares to castle. } 5... Nf6 6. d4 )
5. d4 { Takes the centre. If Black captures, White recaptures with the c-pawn and keeps a big pawn centre. }
5... exd4 6. cxd4 { Recaptures and keeps two pawns in the centre. } 6... Bb6 { The bishop steps out of reach of the d4 pawn and still eyes the diagonal. }
7. Nc3 { Develops and guards e4, so the e-pawn can push to e5 later. }
7... O-O 8. Bd3 { Develops the bishop and clears the way to castle. } 8... Bg4 9. Be3 { Develops the last bishop and guards d4 against ...Bxf3 and ...Nxd4 tricks. Plan: castle, keep the centre pawns together and play e5 when it kicks a piece. If Black leaves the book, complete development before opening lines. } *
